    "created_at": "2021-03-03T15:59:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-03T15:59:21Z",
    "body": "It seems suboptimal to me. I'm fairly convinced that web developers want to treat timeouts differently from aborts (i.e., retry the former, ignore the latter). And we already have a perfectly-good distinction between `\"TimeoutError\"` `DOMException`s and `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException`s, which XHR already uses. So adding a `reason` property to `DOMException` just so that we can reuse `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException` would be confusing, IMO.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
